{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xbjnw8Yp5rUVmzkP9XgoRx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 8 wave(s) planned\n4\t(Wave 1-2 = security hardening H1-H2; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades L1-L6).\n5\t\n6\t## Waves\n7\t\n8\t### Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n9\t\n10\t- **Deliverable:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` â€” re-fetches each scannable artifact's\n11\t  payload (payloads not retained on disk; reuses `fetcher` 7-day cache) and runs the real\n12\t  `payload_extractor.extract â†’ detectors â†’ scorer.score` path, persisting via\n13\t  `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode. Monotonic re-stamp guard delegates to\n14\t  `gate._worst_status` (worst-wins; never raises servability). `--limit/--dry-run/--audit-out`.\n15\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 799 passed (793 after EXECUTE, +6 after FIX; baseline 752).\n16\t  No test weakening. No new `security_status IN (...)` literal (single-owner test green).\n17\t- **Review:** 2 independent reviewers. R1 GO (no blocker). R2 GO with 2 MAJORs:\n18\t  F1 (non-GitHub zero-byte fetch falsely labeled `payload-depth`), F2 (errors didn't gate\n19\t  exit/coverage). FIX iter 1 closed both + 2 MINORs; closure VERIFIER mutation-tested each\n20\t  fix â†’ all CLOSED, invariants intact â†’ GO.\n21\t- **Honesty fix (F1):** only genuinely fetched-and-scanned artifacts get `scan_depth:\n22\t  payload-depth`; no-payload artifacts (â‰ˆ506/775, mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback`\n23\t  and keep their monotonic value (not newly quarantined). Coverage breakdown in the audit.\n24\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** the live re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. Build delivers\n25\t  the CLI + tests only.\n26\t\n27\t### Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n28\t\n29\t- **Deliverables:** real per-iteration LLM `make_live_score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py`\n30\t  (re-runs critic_a/b/c+reconciler over the deepened corpus, metered, never writes the\n31\t  verdict, guards verbatim); `bin/engine-diff.py` (GO/NO-GO enforcing agreementâ‰¥0.95,\n32\t  samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—, strict profile additive); `bin/run_evidence_shadow.py`\n33\t  (budget-capped metered batch â€” SA-1 machinery, not run live); default-off live engine switch\n34\t  `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`.\n35\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 832 passed, 1 pre-existing skip (824 after EXECUTE, +8 after\n36\t  FIX). No test weakening.\n37\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers. Both agreed (â‰¥2 â†’ BLOCKER-class) the nightly shadow path had been\n38\t  swapped to the real score_fn, silently adding per-candidate LLM cost; R2 also reproduced a\n39\t  $0-shadow cost-gate GO. NO-GO â†’ FIX iter 1 closed: nightly defaults to ZERO-cost\n40\t  precomputed score_fn (real re-score behind default-off `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`);\n41\t  $0-shadow â†’ NO-GO; `evidence_shadow` budget cell; live-switch adoption now monotonic-toward-\n42\t  stricter vs legacy (fail-safe). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n43\t- **TRIPWIRE / follow-up:** R2-4 candidate-filter (non-empty bundle) works but lacks a dedicated\n44\t  regression test (LOW). \n45\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** SA-1 (metered shadow batch to populate validations_shadow\n46\t  â‰¥200) and SA-2 (live `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=loop` flip). Default stays legacy; nightly stays\n47\t  zero added cost.\n48\t\n49\t### Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n50\t\n51\t- **Deliverables:** migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` (+ schema.sql mirror) adding nullable\n52\t  `cache_read_tokens`/`cache_write_tokens`/`batch_mode` to `costs`; `kb/pricing.yaml` cache\n53\t  sub-rates (cache_read â‰ˆ0.1Ã—, cache_write â‰ˆ1.25Ã—) for sonnet-4-6 + haiku-4-5 + `batch_discount:\n54\t  0.5`, all provenance-flagged `verified:false`; `llm.py` `lookup_cache_rates`/`batch_discount` +\n55\t  `CostRecorder.record(... cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False)` â€” legacy\n56\t  4-arg path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n57\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 845 passed (+13). No test weakening.\n58\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (legacy unchanged to the cent verified;\n59\t  migration idempotent + applies clean to a live-DB copy preserving 22,013 rows). R2 GO + 5/5\n60\t  mutation-caught tests; one LOW (F2: structural non-slash skip in the verification test) â€”\n61\t  orchestrator-applied an explicit `_NON_RATE_VERIFICATION_KEYS` allowlist so a slash-dropping\n62\t  typo fails loudly; re-gated green.\n63\t- **Note:** migration authored + tested; applied to the live DB by the normal migrate runner (not\n64\t  hand-mutated in the build).\n65\t\n66\t### Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n67\t\n68\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `cache_system` (structured\n69\t  ephemeral system block, cache-read/write metered via L1); invariant rubric/schema moved into the\n70\t  cached system block for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the\n71\t  marker; default (cache-off) path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n72\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 858 passed (854 after EXECUTE, +4 after FIX). No test weakening.\n73\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers. R1 GO (default unchanged, fallback caches, the 3 modified test mocks are\n74\t  faithful signature propagation not weakening). R2 GO with a HIGH efficacy finding (W4-R2-1):\n75\t  cached prefixes (65â€“317 tok) are far below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku\n76\t  4096), so caching silently never fires. FIX iter 1: maximized the stable prefix (moved invariant\n77\t  rubric/schema into system â€” token-multiset identical, F6 fences intact), then GATED the marker\n78\t  behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum` (no dead marker sent) and added honesty-pinning tests.\n79\t  Closure VERIFIER: judge content semantically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n80\t  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n81\t- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n82\t  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n83\t  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n84\t  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n85\t  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n86\t\n87\t### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n88\t\n89\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n90\t  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n91\t  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`RECONCILED_VERDICT_SCHEMA` in contracts.py +\n92\t  `JUDGE_DECISION_SCHEMA`; critic_a/critic_b(Anthropic-fallback)/reconciler/judge pass schemas;\n93\t  Gemini path + langextract untouched. Off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed, enforced by\n94\t  `_parse_response`, not by `strict`).\n95\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 874 passed (869 after EXECUTE, +5 after FIX). No test weakening.\n96\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (fail-closed independently re-verified by the\n97\t  parser). R2 GO-conditional with W5-F1 (MEDIUM): no-`required` strict schema acceptance is\n98\t  unverified against the live API; a rejection would 400 on both Sonnet+Haiku and (since\n99\t  critic/reconciler weren't exception-wrapped) abort the nightly sweep. FIX iter 1: structured call\n100\t  now DEGRADES to a plain text call on any structured-call failure (metered once off the successful\n101\t  call, degrade logged) + defense-in-depth (critic_a/b/reconciler treat a hard call error as\n102\t  degrade-to-None). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n103\t- **TRIPWIRE:** if the live API rejects the no-`required` strict schema, structured outputs silently\n104\t  degrade to the legacy plain-text parse (no benefit, no harm). A one-call live smoke against\n105\t  Sonnet/Haiku would confirm whether the schema activates; until then, treat L3 as best-effort.\n106\t\n107\t### Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n108\t\n109\t- **Deliverables:** `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `effort` (maps to `thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`\n110\t  + `output_config={\"effort\": low|medium|high|xhigh|max}` per the claude-api skill); a recursive\n111\t  `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before EVERY Anthropic dispatch (initial + Haiku fallback +\n112\t  structuredâ†’plain degrade) â€” Opus 4.8 400s on budget_tokens; `_fold_thinking_into_output` folds any\n113\t  separately-reported thinking tokens into metered output (the $118 lesson). Default (effort unset) =\n114\t  cost-neutral, byte-for-byte unchanged. Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard + `thoughts_token_count`\n115\t  fold untouched.\n116\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n117\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n118\t  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n119\t  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n120\t  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n121\t- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n122\t  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n123\t  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n124\t  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n125\t\n126\t### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n127\t\n128\t- **Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` adds `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) with L1-style\n129\t  cache sub-rates + `tokenizer_factor: 1.35` (verified:false); `llm.py` `tokenizer_factor`/\n130\t  `estimate_tokens`/`estimate_usd` estimate-only helpers (factor NEVER touches post-call metering â€”\n131\t  ground-truth invariant, regression-pinned).\n132\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 898 passed (+7). No test weakening.\n133\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (post-call metering provably unfactored;\n134\t  mutation-proven ground-truth test). R2 GO with **honesty findings**: (F1, HIGH-honesty) the\n135\t  estimate helpers are **dead code** â€” no production caller (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token\n136\t  pre-flight), so the tokenizer-factor accuracy goal is not realized; (F2) the defaults were ALREADY\n137\t  on current tiers, so \"retargeting\" changed nothing in the default path. Same inert-plumbing\n138\t  pattern as L2 caching. Corrected an overstated orchestrator comment (F2b).\n139\t- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** L5's concrete value is narrow â€” `claude-opus-4-8` is now priced so\n140\t  an `AURORA_*_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8` override meters correctly instead of $0 (closes a $0-fiction\n141\t  hole on the Opus override path) + a deprecated-Opus guard test. The tokenizer factor + estimate\n142\t  helpers are correct, tested, forward-ready, but **inert until a token-budget pre-flight consumer\n143\t  exists**. (F3, LOW: a future 4.7+ model added without the field silently estimates at 1.0.)\n144\t\n145\t### Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n146\t\n147\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect + `build_anthropic_request_params`\n148\t  (params identical to the synchronous shape incl. L2 cache / L3 tools / L4 effort + budget_tokens\n149\t  guard) + `_meter_batch_result` (records each result `batch_mode=True` â†’ L1's 0.5Ã— from real usage);\n150\t  `roles/batch_sweep.py` opt-in coordinator (`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, default off); critic_a/reconciler\n151\t  refactored into `build_prompt`/`parse_verdict` + a `prefetched_text` param; orchestrator batches\n152\t  critic_a behind the flag. Per-item failure / timeout / missing result â†’ synchronous degrade\n153\t  (`batch_mode=False`, `_note_degrade`); missing security-judge result â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n154\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 915 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n155\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Flag-off path verified byte-for-byte (git-diff-confirmed the\n156\t  critic_a/reconciler parse extraction is verbatim; equivalence also guarded by existing\n157\t  test_structured_outputs + test_critic_c); batch metered exactly 0.5Ã—; per-item degrade + ~65-min\n158\t  poll-timeout-degrade + judge fail-closed all tested; budget_tokens guard runs on batch params.\n159\t- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** like L2/L5, this is **ready plumbing, not a current win**. Only\n160\t  critic_a is wired (1 of 3 per-candidate Anthropic calls, â‰¤400 tokens); reconciler-batch +\n161\t  judge-batch are built+tested but unwired (reconciler has a hard data-dependency on critic output;\n162\t  judge is on the separate gate path). At TOP_K=2 that's ~2 small calls/night â†’ sub-cent savings, and\n163\t  the blocking poll (up to ~65 min) makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` **net-negative EV at current scale**.\n164\t  Default-off is correct; revisit only if TOP_K rises substantially.\n165\t\n166\t---\n167\t\n168\t## Phase 2 â€” PROJECT DONE â€” 2026-06-07\n169\t\n170\tAll 8 planned waves built EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ RE-REVIEW\n171\tand converged GREEN, in order, on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`.\n172\t\n173\t- **Security thread (Wave 1-2, live verdict path):** H1 payload-depth scan (monotonic, honest\n174\t  scan-depth labeling) + H2 evidence-loop promotion machinery (default-legacy, nightly zero-cost,\n175\t  $0-shadowâ†’NO-GO gate, adoption monotonic-toward-stricter). Both real value.\n176\t- **llm.py thread (Wave 3-8):** L1 cost substrate (real, enabling) Â· L3 structured outputs (real\n177\t  robustness + safe degrade) Â· L4 budget_tokens guard + thinking fold (real â€” prevents Opus 4.8 400s,\n178\t  guards the $118 class). **L2 caching / L5 retarget / L6 batch are correct, honest, forward-ready\n179\t  PLUMBING that is largely INERT at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2** â€” exactly the research's\n180\t  \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n181\t- **Ground-truth gate:** `python -m pytest` = **915 passed** (+163 across the 8 waves from the 752\n182\t  Phase-1 baseline). No test weakening anywhere; security suite green throughout.\n183\t- **Locked-preserved intact:** KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost\n184\t  telemetry (post-call metering never altered by any wave), Helping Hand + publisher.\n185\t- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, NOT run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch) + SA-2 (live evidence-engine\n186\t  flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. All gated, default-off.\n187\t- **Commits:** 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4\n188\t  (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· + W8. Not pushed; awaiting John's review.\n189\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a103042a-3a3e-46c5-9f67-f5a4ffa20f84","uuid":"6821e9cb-9652-4d16-97cd-a150ae776102","timestamp":"2026-06-13T12:51:02.366Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-phase2\\EXECUTION-LOG.md","content":"# Aurora Phase 2 â€” Execution Log\n\nForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 8 wave(s) planned\n(Wave 1-2 = security hardening H1-H2; Wave 3-8 = llm.py upgrades L1-L6).\n\n## Waves\n\n### Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n\n- **Deliverable:** `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` â€” re-fetches each scannable artifact's\n  payload (payloads not retained on disk; reuses `fetcher` 7-day cache) and runs the real\n  `payload_extractor.extract â†’ detectors â†’ scorer.score` path, persisting via\n  `gate.write_verdict` in enforce mode. Monotonic re-stamp guard delegates to\n  `gate._worst_status` (worst-wins; never raises servability). `--limit/--dry-run/--audit-out`.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 799 passed (793 after EXECUTE, +6 after FIX; baseline 752).\n  No test weakening. No new `security_status IN (...)` literal (single-owner test green).\n- **Review:** 2 independent reviewers. R1 GO (no blocker). R2 GO with 2 MAJORs:\n  F1 (non-GitHub zero-byte fetch falsely labeled `payload-depth`), F2 (errors didn't gate\n  exit/coverage). FIX iter 1 closed both + 2 MINORs; closure VERIFIER mutation-tested each\n  fix â†’ all CLOSED, invariants intact â†’ GO.\n- **Honesty fix (F1):** only genuinely fetched-and-scanned artifacts get `scan_depth:\n  payload-depth`; no-payload artifacts (â‰ˆ506/775, mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback`\n  and keep their monotonic value (not newly quarantined). Coverage breakdown in the audit.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** the live re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. Build delivers\n  the CLI + tests only.\n\n### Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery â€” GREEN (2026-06-06)\n\n- **Deliverables:** real per-iteration LLM `make_live_score_fn` in `roles/evidence.py`\n  (re-runs critic_a/b/c+reconciler over the deepened corpus, metered, never writes the\n  verdict, guards verbatim); `bin/engine-diff.py` (GO/NO-GO enforcing agreementâ‰¥0.95,\n  samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—, strict profile additive); `bin/run_evidence_shadow.py`\n  (budget-capped metered batch â€” SA-1 machinery, not run live); default-off live engine switch\n  `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 832 passed, 1 pre-existing skip (824 after EXECUTE, +8 after\n  FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers. Both agreed (â‰¥2 â†’ BLOCKER-class) the nightly shadow path had been\n  swapped to the real score_fn, silently adding per-candidate LLM cost; R2 also reproduced a\n  $0-shadow cost-gate GO. NO-GO â†’ FIX iter 1 closed: nightly defaults to ZERO-cost\n  precomputed score_fn (real re-score behind default-off `AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE`);\n  $0-shadow â†’ NO-GO; `evidence_shadow` budget cell; live-switch adoption now monotonic-toward-\n  stricter vs legacy (fail-safe). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n- **TRIPWIRE / follow-up:** R2-4 candidate-filter (non-empty bundle) works but lacks a dedicated\n  regression test (LOW). \n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED (not run):** SA-1 (metered shadow batch to populate validations_shadow\n  â‰¥200) and SA-2 (live `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=loop` flip). Default stays legacy; nightly stays\n  zero added cost.\n\n### Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` (+ schema.sql mirror) adding nullable\n  `cache_read_tokens`/`cache_write_tokens`/`batch_mode` to `costs`; `kb/pricing.yaml` cache\n  sub-rates (cache_read â‰ˆ0.1Ã—, cache_write â‰ˆ1.25Ã—) for sonnet-4-6 + haiku-4-5 + `batch_discount:\n  0.5`, all provenance-flagged `verified:false`; `llm.py` `lookup_cache_rates`/`batch_discount` +\n  `CostRecorder.record(... cache_read_tokens=0, cache_write_tokens=0, batch_mode=False)` â€” legacy\n  4-arg path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 845 passed (+13). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (legacy unchanged to the cent verified;\n  migration idempotent + applies clean to a live-DB copy preserving 22,013 rows). R2 GO + 5/5\n  mutation-caught tests; one LOW (F2: structural non-slash skip in the verification test) â€”\n  orchestrator-applied an explicit `_NON_RATE_VERIFICATION_KEYS` allowlist so a slash-dropping\n  typo fails loudly; re-gated green.\n- **Note:** migration authored + tested; applied to the live DB by the normal migrate runner (not\n  hand-mutated in the build).\n\n### Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `cache_system` (structured\n  ephemeral system block, cache-read/write metered via L1); invariant rubric/schema moved into the\n  cached system block for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the\n  marker; default (cache-off) path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 858 passed (854 after EXECUTE, +4 after FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers. R1 GO (default unchanged, fallback caches, the 3 modified test mocks are\n  faithful signature propagation not weakening). R2 GO with a HIGH efficacy finding (W4-R2-1):\n  cached prefixes (65â€“317 tok) are far below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku\n  4096), so caching silently never fires. FIX iter 1: maximized the stable prefix (moved invariant\n  rubric/schema into system â€” token-multiset identical, F6 fences intact), then GATED the marker\n  behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum` (no dead marker sent) and added honesty-pinning tests.\n  Closure VERIFIER: judge content semantically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n\n### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`RECONCILED_VERDICT_SCHEMA` in contracts.py +\n  `JUDGE_DECISION_SCHEMA`; critic_a/critic_b(Anthropic-fallback)/reconciler/judge pass schemas;\n  Gemini path + langextract untouched. Off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed, enforced by\n  `_parse_response`, not by `strict`).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 874 passed (869 after EXECUTE, +5 after FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (fail-closed independently re-verified by the\n  parser). R2 GO-conditional with W5-F1 (MEDIUM): no-`required` strict schema acceptance is\n  unverified against the live API; a rejection would 400 on both Sonnet+Haiku and (since\n  critic/reconciler weren't exception-wrapped) abort the nightly sweep. FIX iter 1: structured call\n  now DEGRADES to a plain text call on any structured-call failure (metered once off the successful\n  call, degrade logged) + defense-in-depth (critic_a/b/reconciler treat a hard call error as\n  degrade-to-None). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n- **TRIPWIRE:** if the live API rejects the no-`required` strict schema, structured outputs silently\n  degrade to the legacy plain-text parse (no benefit, no harm). A one-call live smoke against\n  Sonnet/Haiku would confirm whether the schema activates; until then, treat L3 as best-effort.\n\n### Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `effort` (maps to `thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`\n  + `output_config={\"effort\": low|medium|high|xhigh|max}` per the claude-api skill); a recursive\n  `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before EVERY Anthropic dispatch (initial + Haiku fallback +\n  structuredâ†’plain degrade) â€” Opus 4.8 400s on budget_tokens; `_fold_thinking_into_output` folds any\n  separately-reported thinking tokens into metered output (the $118 lesson). Default (effort unset) =\n  cost-neutral, byte-for-byte unchanged. Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard + `thoughts_token_count`\n  fold untouched.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n\n### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` adds `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) with L1-style\n  cache sub-rates + `tokenizer_factor: 1.35` (verified:false); `llm.py` `tokenizer_factor`/\n  `estimate_tokens`/`estimate_usd` estimate-only helpers (factor NEVER touches post-call metering â€”\n  ground-truth invariant, regression-pinned).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 898 passed (+7). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (post-call metering provably unfactored;\n  mutation-proven ground-truth test). R2 GO with **honesty findings**: (F1, HIGH-honesty) the\n  estimate helpers are **dead code** â€” no production caller (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token\n  pre-flight), so the tokenizer-factor accuracy goal is not realized; (F2) the defaults were ALREADY\n  on current tiers, so \"retargeting\" changed nothing in the default path. Same inert-plumbing\n  pattern as L2 caching. Corrected an overstated orchestrator comment (F2b).\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** L5's concrete value is narrow â€” `claude-opus-4-8` is now priced so\n  an `AURORA_*_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8` override meters correctly instead of $0 (closes a $0-fiction\n  hole on the Opus override path) + a deprecated-Opus guard test. The tokenizer factor + estimate\n  helpers are correct, tested, forward-ready, but **inert until a token-budget pre-flight consumer\n  exists**. (F3, LOW: a future 4.7+ model added without the field silently estimates at 1.0.)\n\n### Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect + `build_anthropic_request_params`\n  (params identical to the synchronous shape incl. L2 cache / L3 tools / L4 effort + budget_tokens\n  guard) + `_meter_batch_result` (records each result `batch_mode=True` â†’ L1's 0.5Ã— from real usage);\n  `roles/batch_sweep.py` opt-in coordinator (`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, default off); critic_a/reconciler\n  refactored into `build_prompt`/`parse_verdict` + a `prefetched_text` param; orchestrator batches\n  critic_a behind the flag. Per-item failure / timeout / missing result â†’ synchronous degrade\n  (`batch_mode=False`, `_note_degrade`); missing security-judge result â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 915 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Flag-off path verified byte-for-byte (git-diff-confirmed the\n  critic_a/reconciler parse extraction is verbatim; equivalence also guarded by existing\n  test_structured_outputs + test_critic_c); batch metered exactly 0.5Ã—; per-item degrade + ~65-min\n  poll-timeout-degrade + judge fail-closed all tested; budget_tokens guard runs on batch params.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** like L2/L5, this is **ready plumbing, not a current win**. Only\n  critic_a is wired (1 of 3 per-candidate Anthropic calls, â‰¤400 tokens); reconciler-batch +\n  judge-batch are built+tested but unwired (reconciler has a hard data-dependency on critic output;\n  judge is on the separate gate path). At TOP_K=2 that's ~2 small calls/night â†’ sub-cent savings, and\n  the blocking poll (up to ~65 min) makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` **net-negative EV at current scale**.\n  Default-off is correct; revisit only if TOP_K rises substantially.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 â€” PROJECT DONE â€” 2026-06-07\n\nAll 8 planned waves built EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ RE-REVIEW\nand converged GREEN, in order, on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`.\n\n- **Security thread (Wave 1-2, live verdict path):** H1 payload-depth scan (monotonic, honest\n  scan-depth labeling) + H2 evidence-loop promotion machinery (default-legacy, nightly zero-cost,\n  $0-shadowâ†’NO-GO gate, adoption monotonic-toward-stricter). Both real value.\n- **llm.py thread (Wave 3-8):** L1 cost substrate (real, enabling) Â· L3 structured outputs (real\n  robustness + safe degrade) Â· L4 budget_tokens guard + thinking fold (real â€” prevents Opus 4.8 400s,\n  guards the $118 class). **L2 caching / L5 retarget / L6 batch are correct, honest, forward-ready\n  PLUMBING that is largely INERT at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2** â€” exactly the research's\n  \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n- **Ground-truth gate:** `python -m pytest` = **915 passed** (+163 across the 8 waves from the 752\n  Phase-1 baseline). No test weakening anywhere; security suite green throughout.\n- **Locked-preserved intact:** KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost\n  telemetry (post-call metering never altered by any wave), Helping Hand + publisher.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, NOT run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch) + SA-2 (live evidence-engine\n  flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. All gated, default-off.\n- **Commits:** 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4\n  (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· + W8. Not pushed; awaiting John's review.\n","numLines":189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}}}
