{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EsNHT51xwriSj4RJX9yRzt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a grounded summary of the **foreman-handoff-phase2** build trio session, sourced from the three member documents (`DESCRIPTION.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`, `EXECUTION-LOG.md`) anchored by `foreman.config.json`.\n\n## foreman-handoff-phase2 â€” grounded claims\n\n**Scope & framing**\n- This was the *build* half of the researchPrime \"AuroraTwo\" verdict: evolve `llm.py` + the security/evidence path, **not** rebuild the architecture â€” because fan-out is theater at TOP_K=2-3 (per `DESCRIPTION.md:3-7`).\n- Two threads ran in series (they overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge): **security hardening H1-H2** (Waves 1-2) and **llm.py upgrades L1-L6** (Waves 3-8).\n- All 8 waves ran the Foreman loop EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ RE-REVIEW and converged GREEN on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`.\n\n**Security thread (real value)**\n- **W1/H1** â€” `bin/scan_payload_depth.py`: re-fetches each artifact's payload (reusing the 7-day fetcher cache) and runs the real `extract â†’ detectors â†’ scorer.score` path, persisting via `gate.write_verdict`; re-stamp is monotonic (`gate._worst_status`, worst-wins). Honesty fix F1: only genuinely fetched+scanned artifacts get `payload-depth`; the ~506/775 no-payload artifacts (mostly arxiv) get `served-text-fallback` and keep their value.\n- **W2/H2** â€” evidence-loop promotion *machinery*: real metered `make_live_score_fn`, `bin/engine-diff.py` GO/NO-GO gate (agreementâ‰¥0.95, samplesâ‰¥200, unearned==0, costâ‰¤1.5Ã—), budget-capped shadow runner. A BLOCKER-class finding (both reviewers agreed the nightly shadow had silently swapped to the costed score_fn) was fixed: nightly defaults to a **zero-cost precomputed** score_fn; `$0-shadow â†’ NO-GO`; live switch defaults `AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy`.\n\n**llm.py thread â€” real value (L1, L3, L4)**\n- **W3/L1** â€” cost-telemetry substrate: migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` (nullable cache/batch columns), pricing.yaml cache sub-rates + `batch_discount: 0.5` (provenance `verified:false`); legacy 4-arg metering path byte-for-byte unchanged (verified to the cent, idempotent against a 22,013-row live-DB copy).\n- **W5/L3** â€” structured outputs via strict forced tool-use (`emit_result`); shared verdict/judge schemas; **degrades to plain-text on any structured-call failure** and off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n- **W6/L4** â€” adaptive `effort` thinking + a recursive `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard before every Anthropic dispatch (Opus 4.8 400s on `budget_tokens`) + `_fold_thinking_into_output` (guards the \"$118 lesson\"). Default path cost-neutral.\n\n**llm.py thread â€” honest inert plumbing (L2, L5, L6)**\n- **W4/L2 prompt caching** is a **no-op at current prompt sizes** â€” stable prefixes (15-60 tok) are 15-60Ã— below model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku 4096); plumbing is correct and gated behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum`, but no savings banked. This refines the research's #1 \"cheap win\" to *inapplicable at current size*.\n- **W5â†’W7/L5 retargeting**: estimate helpers (`tokenizer_factor` 1.35, `estimate_tokens/usd`) are **dead code** (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, no token pre-flight consumer); the one real win is pricing `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) so an Opus override meters correctly instead of $0. Factor never touches post-call metering (ground-truth invariant, regression-pinned).\n- **W8/L6 Message Batches**: full submit/poll/collect + `roles/batch_sweep.py` built and tested, but only critic_a is wired; at TOP_K=2 it's ~2 small calls/night and the ~65-min blocking poll makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` **net-negative EV**. Default-off correct.\n\n**Gate, invariants, status**\n- Ground-truth gate `python -m pytest`: **915 passed** at project-done, **+163** over the 752 Phase-1 baseline; **no te